From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:26:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Navigation cache rebuild: the splash loop sleeps as long
 as its frames take

While the navigation cache is rebuilt in its thread, fgInitNav() returns to
the main loop after a sleep of 50 msec, and the main loop draws a frame of
the splash screen. Where that frame takes seconds (software rendering on one
CPU) the rebuild thread gets a small part of the processor. The sleep is now
three times the time the frame before took, between 50 msec and 5 s, so the
rebuild has three quarters of the time whatever a frame costs; with frames
of 16 msec nothing changes.

Measured on AROS in QEMU/KVM with one CPU on the softpipe GL driver,
1024x768: "cache rebuild took" 904 s, against 2188 s with the fixed 50 msec
(one run each).
---
 src/Main/fg_init.cxx | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Main/fg_init.cxx b/src/Main/fg_init.cxx
index e6c0891..1551440 100755
--- a/src/Main/fg_init.cxx
+++ b/src/Main/fg_init.cxx
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 
 #include <simgear/compiler.h>
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstdlib>
 #include <cstring>             // strcmp()
@@ -1006,8 +1007,19 @@ fgInitNav ()
             fgSplashProgress(splashIdentsByRebuildPhase[phase],
                              cache->rebuildPhaseCompletionPercentage());
 
-            // sleep to give the rebuild thread more time
-            SGTimeStamp::sleepForMSec(50);
+            // sleep to give the rebuild thread more time: three times as long as the frame
+            // before took to draw. Where a frame of the splash screen takes seconds (software
+            // rendering, one CPU) 50 msec left the thread a fortieth of the time.
+            static SGTimeStamp lastCall;
+            static int lastSleepMSec = 0;
+            int sleepMSec = 50;
+            if (lastSleepMSec > 0) {
+                const int frameMSec = lastCall.elapsedMSec() - lastSleepMSec;
+                sleepMSec = std::min(std::max(3 * frameMSec, 50), 5000);
+            }
+            lastCall.stamp();
+            lastSleepMSec = sleepMSec;
+            SGTimeStamp::sleepForMSec(sleepMSec);
             return false;
         }
     }
